# The keys whose signature makes a Seamless release TAG: an OpenSSH
# allowed_signers file (ssh-keygen(1), ALLOWED SIGNERS), namespace git.
#
# scripts/release/macos.sh signs the release tag vX.Y.Z (its message is the
# macOS assets' sha256 manifest) with the release signing helper, and then
# checks it against this file, with /usr/bin/ssh-keygen, never the one on
# PATH and never the owner's global allowed_signers. scripts/release/sign.sh
# checks the tag the same way before it signs checksums.txt. Both refuse to
# run on a dirty tree, so the list they check against is the one HEAD holds.
#
# These are the same two hardware keys release_signers lists for
# checksums.txt, in namespace git here. A fork that signs its own release
# tags lists its own keys here.
